    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n**Change** \u2014 I reused the existing `displayName` idiom rather than adding logic to any entity class:\n\n1. `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field).\n2. `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation to `toOwnerDto` computing initials by expression:\n   `Character.toUpperCase(firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\"` \u2192 e.g. `J.S.`\n\n**Structural impact:** 2 files; the only function touched is `toOwnerDto` (CC 1, one added annotation line), sitting in an interface of simple CC-1 methods. No entity or endpoint pipeline was modified, and no method grew in complexity.",
